The development of connected orthopedic technologies reflects growing interest in personalized rehabilitation, objective postoperative assessment, and data-supported clinical decision-making.
As healthcare systems seek improved visibility into patient recovery and manufacturers develop increasingly sophisticated orthopedic devices, sensor-enabled joint implants present new opportunities for medical technology innovation.
